.TH POLEZEROS 1
.SH NAME
polezeros \- a transfer function, coloured
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/polezeros
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I PoleZeros
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/PoleZeros.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
Every pixel of the window is a point in the complex plane, and its colour
is the magnitude of the rational function whose roots are two zeros and
whose poles are two poles \- the picture engineers draw as a pole-zero
plot, except that this is the surface itself rather than a diagram of it.
Holding the right button swaps magnitude for phase.
.PP
The scale is not chosen.  The program renders, sums what it drew,
rescales and renders again, stopping when the total stops moving, which
is an auto-exposure loop and is why the picture looks right for any
arrangement of poles you drag them into.
.PP
Dragging picks whichever pole or zero is nearest the cursor by squared
distance and moves it.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B LMB
Drag the nearest pole or zero
.TP
.B RMB
Show phase instead of magnitude
.TP
.B "any key"
Exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/polezeros.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
